            <header class="lesson-header"><span class="lesson-number">Lesson 11</span><h1>Concurrency Handling</h1><div class="lesson-meta"><span class="lesson-duration"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"/><polyline points="12 6 12 12 16 14"/></svg>25 min</span><span class="lesson-level intermediate">Intermediate</span></div></header>
            <div class="lesson-body">
                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>The Concurrency Problem</h2>
                    <p>When two users edit the same record simultaneously, whose changes win? Without handling, the last save overwrites all previous changes.</p>
                </section>

                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>Concurrency Tokens</h2>
                    <pre><code class="language-csharp">public class Product
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string Name { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public decimal Price { get; set; }
    
    [ConcurrencyCheck]
    public decimal Stock { get; set; }
}

// Fluent API
modelBuilder.Entity&lt;Product&gt;()
    .Property(p =&gt; p.Stock)
    .IsConcurrencyToken();</code></pre>
                </section>

                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>RowVersion (Recommended)</h2>
                    <pre><code class="language-csharp">public class Product
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string Name { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    
    [Timestamp]
    public byte[] RowVersion { get; set; } = null!;
}

// Fluent API
modelBuilder.Entity&lt;Product&gt;()
    .Property(p =&gt; p.RowVersion)
    .IsRowVersion();</code></pre>
                    <p>SQL Server automatically updates RowVersion on every change.</p>
                </section>

                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>Handling Conflicts</h2>
                    <pre><code class="language-csharp">try
{
    await context.SaveChangesAsync();
}
catch (DbUpdateConcurrencyException ex)
{
    foreach (var entry in ex.Entries)
    {
        var proposedValues = entry.CurrentValues;
        var databaseValues = await entry.GetDatabaseValuesAsync();

        if (databaseValues == null)
        {
            // Entity was deleted
            throw new InvalidOperationException("Record was deleted");
        }

        // Option 1: Database wins
        entry.OriginalValues.SetValues(databaseValues);
        
        // Option 2: Client wins
        entry.OriginalValues.SetValues(databaseValues);
        // Keep proposed values, try save again
        
        // Option 3: Merge values
        foreach (var property in proposedValues.Properties)
        {
            var proposedValue = proposedValues[property];
            var databaseValue = databaseValues[property];
            // Custom merge logic here
        }
    }
    
    // Retry save
    await context.SaveChangesAsync();
}</code></pre>
                </section>

                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>Conflict Resolution Strategies</h2>
                    <div class="comparison-grid">
                        <div class="comparison-card">
                            <h4>Database Wins</h4>
                            <p>Discard user changes, reload from database.</p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="comparison-card">
                            <h4>Client Wins</h4>
                            <p>Force overwrite with user's changes.</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="comparison-grid">
                        <div class="comparison-card">
                            <h4>Merge</h4>
                            <p>Compare and merge individual properties.</p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="comparison-card">
                            <h4>User Decides</h4>
                            <p>Show conflict UI, let user resolve.</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </section>

                <section class="lesson-section">
                    <h2>Key Takeaways</h2>
                    <div class="takeaways">
                        <div class="takeaway"><svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg><span>Concurrency tokens detect conflicting updates.</span></div>
                        <div class="takeaway"><svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg><span>RowVersion is the most reliable approach.</span></div>
                        <div class="takeaway"><svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg><span>DbUpdateConcurrencyException signals conflicts.</span></div>
                        <div class="takeaway"><svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><polyline points="20 6 9 17 4 12"/></svg><span>Choose resolution strategy based on business needs.</span></div>
                    </div>
